    {
      "skill_id": "de-a2-014",
      "title": "Adjective endings after common articles",
      "explanation": "An adjective before a noun takes an ending. After the definite article (nominative and feminine, neuter or plural accusative) the ending is -e: der große Tisch, die neue Lampe, das alte Haus. After the indefinite article the ending shows the gender: ein großer Tisch, eine neue Lampe, ein altes Haus. In the masculine accusative the ending is -en: Ich kaufe einen großen Tisch. The ending carries the case information that the article does not.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Der große Tisch ist neu.",
          "en": "The big table is new."
        },
        {
          "de": "Ich kaufe eine neue Lampe.",
          "en": "I am buying a new lamp."
        },
        {
          "de": "Wir haben ein altes Haus.",
          "en": "We have an old house."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["GOETHE-A2-FIT", "GOETHE-A2-ADULT", "GOETHE-DO-A2"],
